:null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nReproducible in `4.5.stable`\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.5.stable - Windows 11 (build 26100) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce GTX 1660 SUPER (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.7652) - Intel(R) Core(TM) i7-10700F CPU @ 2.90GHz (16 threads) - 15.92 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\n4.5 introduced replaces the `Run Scene` button and the `Run Specific Scene` button with popup menus that allow the user to select between running in regular mode and running in XR mode.\n\nWhile having this choice is nice, it does mean that it is now impossible to press a button or a key to run the scene. An additional action is now required. Sometimes, two additional actions are required, because the last-used option is sometimes highlighted, but sometimes not. This means the user cannot even adjust to the new UX by remembering to press two keys in a row, because sometimes it needs more. This also means I can no longer put on my headset and hit a key using muscle memory to hop in. I'm now forced to start the game *before* putting on my headset (which is problematic because sometimes I need to test something that happens right when the game starts).\n\nThe keyboard shortcuts are now functionally equivalent to _opening a dropdown_. This is not how shortcuts are typically used in the Godot editor - they are supposed to *perform an operation* or *open a feature*.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n- Have an XR headset connected.\n- Press F6 (or whatever the Run Scene shortcut is mapped to).\n- Note that the dropdown opens, but you need to make an additional selection to start the game.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A","closed_by":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://av